>
> Geodesic domes are half-spheres composed out of triangles, does that
> help???


Except that they're not.  Specifically, not just any arrangement of
triangles would not necessarily be geodesic.  The important thing about the
design is that the struts form lines that are straight in relationship to
the curved surface.

I think I like {sirzargu boldi'u} more and more.  Nice, concise, and with a
slightly risque metaphor.

